WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.924 --> 00:00:08.067
For the rest of the day, Daisy and Kaleem tried to find a home for Scamp.

2
00:00:08.087 --> 00:00:43.941
They knocked on every door in the Many of the neighbors knew Scamp and liked him.

3
00:00:46.742 --> 00:00:48.103
But nobody would adopt him.

4
00:00:48.123 --> 00:00:53.205
"I'm sorry, but my cats wouldn't approve," a man said.

5
00:00:53.225 --> 00:00:56.466
A pair of cats stared out from behind him.

6
00:00:56.486 --> 00:00:58.767
"Right," one said.

7
00:00:58.787 --> 00:01:00.868
"We don't like dogs."

8
00:01:01.749 --> 00:01:04.530
Daisy wanted to tell the cats that Scamp was nice.

9
00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:07.291
But she couldn't do it in front of their owner.

10
00:01:08.172 --> 00:01:12.389
Besides, how would she convince the owner without giving away her secret?

11
00:01:17.751 --> 00:01:22.532
wish I could tell people that I can talk to animals," she said as they walked away from

12
00:01:22.572 --> 00:01:23.012
the house.

13
00:01:23.952 --> 00:01:27.673
"Maybe then they'd understand how upset Scamp is and adopt him."

14
00:01:27.693 --> 00:01:29.774
"What? No!"

15
00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:31.695
Beatrice sounded alarmed.

16
00:01:31.715 --> 00:01:33.875
"You can't tell anyone, Daisy!

17
00:01:34.395 --> 00:01:36.116
Besides, you know how adults are.

18
00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.582
They'll think you're playing a silly game and never believe you."

19
00:01:41.043 --> 00:01:41.964
Daisy sighed.

20
00:01:43.124 --> 00:01:45.526
Beatrice was so confusing sometimes.

21
00:01:46.026 --> 00:01:48.968
But right now she had a bigger problem to solve.

22
00:01:48.988 --> 00:01:52.030
"Kaleem, let's try the next house."

23
00:01:56.974 --> 00:01:59.636
By Sunday, they still hadn't found a home for Scamp.

24
00:02:12.482 --> 00:02:16.203
Daisy and Kaleem met in her backyard after breakfast.

25
00:02:16.223 --> 00:02:20.385
"I don't know what to do," she said.

26
00:02:20.405 --> 00:02:22.666
"Poor Scamp!

27
00:02:23.146 --> 00:02:25.647
I guess he's going with the rescue group tomorrow."

28
00:02:26.848 --> 00:02:28.048
Beatrice buzzed over.

29
00:02:28.068 --> 00:02:31.029
"You can't give up, Daisy.

30
00:02:31.469 --> 00:02:32.430
Keep thinking.

31
00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:34.111
Time is running out!"

32
00:02:35.471 --> 00:02:36.331
"Let's visit Mrs.

33
00:02:36.391 --> 00:02:38.704
Ortiz in the hospital," Kaleem said.

34
00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:40.765
"Maybe she'll have some ideas."

35
00:02:48.628 --> 00:02:50.789
Kaleem's dad dropped them off at the hospital.

36
00:02:55.111 --> 00:02:57.072
He was going to park the car and wait for them.

37
00:03:05.255 --> 00:03:06.876
Grace's friends!"

38
00:03:07.444 --> 00:03:09.706
Mrs. Ortiz said when the kids entered.

39
00:03:09.726 --> 00:03:13.688
"Thank you for looking after Scamp."

40
00:03:15.029 --> 00:03:17.071
"We've been trying to find a home for him."

41
00:03:17.571 --> 00:03:18.592
Daisy told Mrs.

42
00:03:18.652 --> 00:03:21.594
Ortiz about talking to Grace's parents and the neighbors.

43
00:03:23.095 --> 00:03:24.636
Mrs. Ortiz looked sad.

44
00:03:24.656 --> 00:03:30.479
"I wish I could keep him, even though he'll be happier with someone younger.

45
00:03:30.499 --> 00:03:33.922
I was hoping Grace would adopt him.

46
00:03:34.562 --> 00:03:36.984
But Scamp can't be around those fish.

47
00:03:38.044 --> 00:03:40.867
And that tank is already a lot of work."

48
00:03:42.168 --> 00:03:44.590
"We were hoping that too," Daisy said.

49
00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:46.431
Mrs. Ortiz sighed.

50
00:03:46.451 --> 00:03:51.876
"I'm sorry for the stress this will cause him.

51
00:03:52.436 --> 00:03:56.980
And I must admit, I'm feeling a little sorry for myself too."

52
00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.422
"You mean because you'll miss Scamp?"

53
00:03:59.842 --> 00:04:00.743
Kaleem asked.

54
00:04:01.644 --> 00:04:02.664
The old woman nodded.

55
00:04:02.684 --> 00:04:06.608
"Yes. I've always had an animal or two around.

56
00:04:08.244 --> 00:04:11.546
I'm looking forward to seeing more of my grandkids.

57
00:04:13.027 --> 00:04:16.929
But they'll be at school all day, and their parents will be at work.

58
00:04:17.549 --> 00:04:21.651
I'm afraid I'll be terribly bored in that condo by myself."

59
00:04:22.992 --> 00:04:24.293
She glanced toward the window.

60
00:04:24.313 --> 00:04:27.855
"I suppose I'll have to settle for bird-watching.

61
00:04:28.275 --> 00:04:31.997
But that's not the same as being able to fuss over a pet of your own.

62
00:04:33.278 --> 00:04:35.179
I like taking care of something.

63
00:04:35.779 --> 00:04:37.260
Maybe I'll get some fish."

64
00:04:38.528 --> 00:04:40.049
Daisy gasped.

65
00:04:40.069 --> 00:04:42.911
"No!" Kaleem looked surprised.

66
00:04:42.931 --> 00:04:44.853
"What do you have against fish?"

67
00:04:44.873 --> 00:04:46.594
"It's not that.

68
00:04:47.175 --> 00:04:48.616
I have an even better idea."

69
00:04:49.376 --> 00:04:50.777
Daisy smiled at Mrs.

70
00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:53.359
Ortiz. "We have to go now.

71
00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:56.642
But I'm hoping I'll be back soon with good news!"
